+# Implementation Plan: JSON Pointer resolution
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Summary
+Single module `src/pointer.ts` with `resolvePointer`, re-exported from `src/index.ts`. Parse pointer into decoded tokens, then walk the document.
+
+## Technical Context
+TypeScript (strict, ES2022, NodeNext), no runtime dependencies, tests with `node --test`.
+
+## Constitution Check
+Constitution is an unfilled template: no rules to violate. Library behaviour follows RFC 6901.
+
+## Structure
+- `src/pointer.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `test/pointer.test.ts`
+
+## Decisions
+- Own-property lookup via `Object.hasOwn`; array index regex `^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$`.
+- `-` is valid syntax but never resolves on existing documents → throws.
